    "summary": "The PR moves the download language from the request query string (`lang`) into the `lang` option of the shared `fetch` helper for three download-stream methods: ConsumerApi CSV and pivot streams and PublisherApi preview stream. This is intended to stop the page-level locale from overwriting the explicitly selected download language. The e2e spec adds a check that a Welsh CSV download differs from the English one and contains a Welsh header marker. Reviewers should focus on whether the `Locale` type assertion is safe for all callers and on whether the `fetch` helper reliably propagates the supplied language for every stream format, not just CSV.",
